    "            <div class='place-body'>",
    "              <h4>4. Mount Batulao</h4>",
    "              <p><strong>Location:</strong> Nasugbu, Batangas, CALABARZON, Philippines</p>",
    "              <p><strong>Google Rating:</strong> 4.6 (139 reviews) — <em>By Wikipedia</em></p>",
    "<p><strong>Photo:</strong> <a href='https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mount_Batulao.jpg' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>Dionisia.besas (CC BY-SA 4.0)</a></p>",
    "              <p>Mount Batulao is an inactive andesitic stratovolcano located in Nasugbu, Batangas, near the Cavite border and Tagaytay Ridge.</p>",
    "              <h5>Natural attractions</h5>",
    "              <ul>",
    "                <li>Rolling grassland ridges</li>",
    "                <li>Jagged peaks and knife-edge trails</li>",
    "                <li>Illuminated rock formations</li>",
    "                <li>Dipterocarp forest sanctuary</li>",
    "              </ul>",
    "              <h5>Things to do</h5>",
    "              <ul>",
    "                <li>Day hiking and traversing</li>",
    "                <li>Ridge scrambling and rappelling</li>",
    "                <li>Overnight camping and sunrise chasing</li>",
    "                <li>Landscape photography and birdwatching</li>",
    "              </ul>",
    "              <h5>Nearby tourist spots</h5>",
    "              <ul>",
    "                <li>Caleruega Church, particularly the Transfiguration Chapel, located near the base of Mount Batulao</li>",
    "              </ul>",
    "              <h5>Travel preparations</h5>",
    "              <ul>",
    "                <li>Prepare for a beginner-to-moderate climb at 811 meters above sea level, with open rolling slopes, ridge walks, and steep rock-scrambling sections.</li>",
    "              </ul>",
    "              <h5>Safety guideline</h5>",
    "              <p>Prepare for the trail conditions, follow local requirements, and be careful along the steep ridges and rock-scrambling sections. Mount Batulao is a beginner-friendly climb with a difficulty level of 4/9, featuring 12 to 13 rolling peaks and open ridge trails.</p>",
    "              <div class='place-actions'>",
    "                <a class='button' href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/resorts%20near%20Mount%20Batulao%20Nasugbu%2C%20Batangas' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' aria-label='Find resorts near Mount Batulao'>Nearby resorts</a>",
    "                <a class='button' href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Mount%20Batulao%20Nasugbu%2C%20Batangas' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' aria-label='Get directions to Mount Batulao'>Get directions</a>",
    "              </div>",
    "            </div>",
    "          </article>",
