    "          <!-- 6. Mount Banahaw -->",
    "          <article class='place-card searchable' data-search='Mount Banahaw Boundary of Laguna and Quezon Province, CALABARZON Mountains Luzon'>",
    "            <img src='images/destinations/luzon-mountain-6.jpg' alt='Mount Banahaw rising above Sampaloc Lake in Laguna.' loading='lazy' onerror=\"this.outerHTML='<div class=&quot;image-fallback&quot;>Mount Banahaw photo</div>'\">",
    "            <div class='place-body'>",
    "              <h4>6. Mount Banahaw</h4>",
    "              <p><strong>Location:</strong> Boundary of Laguna and Quezon Province, CALABARZON, Luzon, Philippines</p>",
    "              <p><strong>Google Rating:</strong> 4.5 (252 reviews) — <em>By Wikipedia</em></p>",
    "<p><strong>Photo:</strong> <a href='https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sampaloc_Lake,_P._Gomez,_Mount_Banahaw_drone_(San_Pablo,_Laguna;_05-16-2026).jpg' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer'>Patrickroque01 (CC BY-SA 4.0)</a></p>",
    "              <p>Mount Banahaw is an active complex volcano located between Laguna and Quezon provinces. Standing at 2,170 meters, it is the tallest peak in the CALABARZON region. It is also known as a sacred mountain where religious traditions and natural beauty come together.</p>",
    "              <h5>Natural attractions</h5>",
    "              <ul>",
    "                <li>Mossy montane forests</li>",
    "                <li>Sacred springs and waterfalls</li>",
    "                <li>Volcanic caves</li>",
    "              </ul>",
    "              <h5>Things to do</h5>",
    "              <ul>",
    "                <li>Spiritual pilgrimages</li>",
    "                <li>Eco-trekking and river caving</li>",
    "                <li>Agro-tourism and birdwatching</li>",
    "              </ul>",
    "              <h5>Nearby tourist spots</h5>",
    "              <ul>",
    "                <li>Sta. Lucia Falls</li>",
    "                <li>Kinabuhayan Shrines and Caves</li>",
    "                <li>Bangkong Kahit Valley</li>",
    "              </ul>",
    "              <h5>Travel preparations</h5>",
    "              <ul>",
    "                <li>Coordinate with local tourism offices for trail access and fees.</li>",
    "                <li>Prepare through light cardio and endurance exercises, and bring a headlamp or flashlight for dark caves and forest trails.</li>",
    "              </ul>",
    "              <h5>Safety guideline</h5>",
    "              <p>The summit and inner caldera are closed to the public. Secure permits before entering, hire an authorized local guide, and bring trash bags to carry your waste out of the protected forest. Bring enough cash, extra clothes, and a quick-dry towel, and use waterproof bags to protect your belongings from sudden rain and water activities.</p>",
    "              <div class='place-actions'>",
    "                <a class='button' href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/resorts%20near%20Mount%20Banahaw%20Laguna%2C%20Philippines' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' aria-label='Find resorts near Mount Banahaw'>Nearby resorts</a>",
    "                <a class='button' href='https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Mount%20Banahaw%20Laguna%2C%20Philippines' target='_blank' rel='noopener noreferrer' aria-label='Get directions to Mount Banahaw'>Get directions</a>",
    "              </div>",
    "            </div>",
    "          </article>",
